<section
  class="clear-instrument model"
  id="model"
  data-instrument="model"
  aria-labelledby="model-title"
>
  <header class="instrument-heading">
    <p class="code">02 / THE MODEL</p>
    <span class="instrument-state" data-model-state>
      MODEL DEPENDENT
    </span>
  </header>
  <div class="model-heading">
    <h2 id="model-title">
      A beautiful
      <br />
      <em>explanation.</em>
    </h2>
    <p class="field-invitation">
      Turn the mechanism.
      <br />
      Then move its centre.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="model-composition">
    <div
      class="phenomenon orbit-field"
      data-orbit-field
      role="slider"
      tabindex="0"
      aria-label="Turn the orbital mechanism to change elapsed day"
      aria-valuemin="0"
      aria-valuemax="780"
      aria-valuenow="0"
      aria-valuetext="Day zero in an illustrative orbit record"
    >
      <svg data-orbit-svg viewBox="0 0 600 500" aria-hidden="true">
        <g class="orbit-graduations" data-orbit-graduations></g>
        <circle
          class="orbit-time-marker"
          data-orbit-time-marker
          cx="530"
          cy="240"
          r="5"
        />
        <circle class="deferent" data-deferent cx="300" cy="240" r="134.1" />
        <circle
          class="earth-orbit is-erased"
          data-earth-orbit
          cx="300"
          cy="240"
          r="88"
        />
        <circle class="epicycle" data-epicycle cx="434.1" cy="240" r="88" />
        <path class="orbital-trace" data-orbital-trace />
        <path class="construction-arm" data-construction-arm />
        <path class="line-of-sight" data-line-of-sight />
        <g class="model-sun" data-model-sun>
          <circle r="9" />
          <path d="M-16 0H-12M12 0H16M0-16V-12M0 12V16" />
        </g>
        <g class="model-earth" data-model-earth>
          <circle r="7" />
          <circle class="observer-ring" r="17" />
        </g>
        <circle class="deferent-centre" data-deferent-centre r="4" />
        <g class="model-planet" data-model-planet>
          <circle r="7" />
          <circle r="15" />
        </g>
        <text class="orbit-label" data-earth-label>
          EARTH / OBSERVER
        </text>
        <text class="orbit-label" data-sun-label>
          SUN
        </text>
        <text class="orbit-label" data-planet-label>
          MARS
        </text>
        <text class="orbit-label" data-epicycle-label>
          EPICYCLE
        </text>
        <text x="300" y="484" text-anchor="middle" class="orbit-drag-label">
          TURN THE RIM / EACH DIVISION = 30 DAYS
        </text>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="model-register">
      <p class="code">THE SAME SYNTHETIC SKY</p>
      <svg
        class="sky-record"
        viewBox="0 0 220 175"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Observed sky bearings in white; predicted bearings in blue"
      >
        <path d="M25 138H195M110 24V151" />
        <g data-sky-observations></g>
        <g data-sky-predictions></g>
      </svg>
      <p class="record-key">
        <span>● RECORD</span>
        <span>+ PREDICTION</span>
      </p>
      <dl class="model-measures">
        <div>
          <dt>ELAPSED</dt>
          <dd>
            <output data-model-day>0</output> days
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>ANGULAR RMS ERROR</dt>
          <dd>
            <output data-model-error>0.00°</output>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>TESTED BEARINGS</dt>
          <dd>48 synthetic samples</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <div
        class="frame-choices"
        role="group"
        aria-label="Choose the origin of the coordinate frame"
      >
        <button type="button" data-model-frame="earth" aria-pressed="true">
          <span class="frame-earth" aria-hidden="true">
            ⊕
          </span>{" "}
          EARTH CENTRED
        </button>
        <button type="button" data-model-frame="sun" aria-pressed="false">
          <span class="frame-sun" aria-hidden="true">
            ☉
          </span>{" "}
          SUN CENTRED
        </button>
      </div>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="text-action fold-epicycle"
        data-model-simplify
        aria-pressed="false"
      >
        ERASE THE EPICYCLE TERM ↗
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="model-equation">
    <span class="code">POSITION SEEN FROM EARTH</span>
    <p data-model-equation>
      deferent <em>−</em> epicycle <em>=</em> apparent position
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="revelation" aria-live="polite">
    <p class="signal" data-model-signal>
      THE MODEL IS NOT THE THING
    </p>
    <p class="revelation-line" data-model-reveal>
      What does prediction prove?
    </p>
    <p class="revelation-detail" data-model-detail>
      White points retain the reference record. Blue marks show the prediction.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="instrument-notes">
    <a href="/models/replace-stories-with-systems.html">
      OPEN MODEL / REPLACE STORIES WITH SYSTEMS ↗
    </a>
    <details>
      <summary>UNSEAL THE ASSUMPTIONS</summary>
      <p>
        A simplified Ptolemaic-style deferent and epicycle, compared with a
        Sun-centred circular construction. The two complete constructions are
        the same vector relation in different coordinate frames. Their exact
        agreement is mathematical, not independent evidence for two physical
        cosmologies.
      </p>
      <p>
        Earth: 1 AU, 365.256 days. Mars: 1.524 AU, 686.98 days. Uniform,
        coplanar circles; no eccentricity, equant, inclination, perturbations or
        light-time correction. This is not a reconstruction of Ptolemy’s full
        machinery or a modern ephemeris.
      </p>
      <p>
        RMS compares 48 directions over a fixed 780-day illustrative record.
        Erasing the Earth-motion term is a deliberate loss of mechanism.
        Historical geocentrism and heliocentrism are distinguishable by evidence
        beyond these projected directions.
      </p>
      <div class="source-links">
        <a href="https://sciencedemonstrations.fas.harvard.edu/presentations/ptolemaic-epicycle-machine">
          HARVARD / EPICYCLE MACHINE ↗
        </a>
        <a href="https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/marsfact.html">
          NASA / ORBIT PARAMETERS ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
